{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEpic 62dc's criterion 5 is undelivered: plan review never tells a reviewer that the plan under review overlaps work another ticket describes. Each plan is read in isolation, so two tickets planning one change both pass.\n\nCreate-time surfacing matches a title plus a short description; plan review runs later against a full plan, far more material. One index serves both.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Reuse the index; add no second retrieval path.** The sibling story builds a lexical FTS5 index under `.rebar/cache/similar-tickets/`, caught up in the read phase, no daemon. Its whole public surface is `find_similar` (`src/rebar/similar/__init__.py:46-54`, stated at `:8`). It takes query text via `text=` (`:51`, resolved at `:73`) plus `exclude_id=` to drop self-hits (`:52`), so querying it with plan material needs no new retrieval module. With the optional embedding tier configured it ranks through that tier, otherwise lexically (`:79-82`): no model provider is required.\n\n**The one gap: failure distinguishability.** Every failure returns `[]`, per \"Never raises\" (`:55`), so a caller cannot tell an absent index from a failed catch-up from an empty match.\n\n**Diagnostic contract.** `find_similar` gains one keyword-only parameter `diagnostics: dict | None = None`. When a dict is passed it records a `status` plus a human `detail`. The set is closed because it is one value per branch: `index-absent` `:63`, `catch-up-failed` `:66-71`, `retrieval-error` at the outer handler `:84`, else `ok` (`:80` embedding, `:82` lexical). An embedding-provider failure is NOT a status: `embedding.rank` returns `None` for every cause it cannot serve -- unconfigured, backend absent, provider failing, coverage incomplete (`:76-79`) -- and `:82` then serves lexical results, so that path is `ok`. Return type, \"Never raises\", every existing call stay unchanged: the signal travels through the dict, not the return value. The only `src/` consumer is the create path at `src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py:196` (imported `:27`), which passes no `diagnostics`.\n\n**Recording channel: coverage, written in place.** `run_pass1` takes `coverage` as a mutable dict (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:238`) and assigns diagnostic keys into it directly -- `coverage[\"isf\"]` `:473`, `coverage[\"recall_candidates\"]` `:521`; `coverage[\"overlap\"]` is written the same way. `coverage_extra` is not the seam: it belongs to `indeterminate_verdict` (`claimability.py:132`), reached only on the LLM-skipping early returns the overlap path never takes.\n\n**Ride the existing Pass-1 extra-context seam.** A Pass-1 finder unit already accepts store-derived `extra_context` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/checkpoints.py:54`), its identity binding that context by `context_digest`, a sha256 over the injected text (`:61-63`, carried at `:70`), under the discovery contract `plan_review_findings` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py:122`). That text is built by `_chunk_extra_context` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:215`), whose single call site `:326` feeds `_discovery_unit_plan` `:331` plus `checkpoint_identity` `:339`, so injection lands in `pass1.py`. The seam is live: `:219-222` already injects G5 decomposition context. Appending candidates there rather than adding a pass keeps checkpoint identity and caching unchanged: a changed candidate set yields a different `context_digest`.\n\n**Zero marginal LLM cost: the existing Pass-1 unit does the judging.** Candidates ride a chunk already being sent, so overlap judging adds no LLM call; lexical retrieval is not one either. The cap is therefore on candidates, not calls. It is 5, the default `RESULT_LIMIT` (`src/rebar/similar/lexical.py:39`): ADR 0122 makes k=5 load-bearing, not an implementation detail -- at k=10 the vector tier's advantage vanishes into noise -- so overlap keeps that operating point rather than forcing a `--paired` re-run.\n\n**On demand, not on every review.** The switch is one keyword-only parameter `overlap: bool = False` on `review_plan` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:199`). `review_plan` does not call `run_pass1`: its only `src/` caller is `ProductionBatchRunner.run`, which builds the call at `production_batch_runner.py:152` from a `BatchRunRequest`. So `overlap` rides `req.with_inputs` -- the seam already carrying `probe_criteria` (`:123`) and `relation_snapshot` (`:157`) -- set where the batch request is assembled, read in `ProductionBatchRunner.run`, passed to `run_pass1` (`pass1.py:232`), then to `_chunk_extra_context`. Default off: without `overlap=True` nothing is injected.\n\n**The injected block carries its decision rule.** Mirroring `decomposition_state_block` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_lint.py:46`), `overlap.py` emits a `## POSSIBLE OVERLAP (from store)` heading, then a directive: judge whether this plan does work a listed ticket already describes; emit one advisory finding per overlapping candidate naming its id and why; emit none when nothing overlaps; never block. Then one `alias -- title (status)` line per candidate, the shape at `:66-70`. Advisory because a child, a follow-up, a split all overlap by construction.\n\n**Degradation.** On any non-`ok` status the candidate list is empty and no overlap finding is emitted, the review proceeding to its normal verdict.\n\n**The injection site has little headroom, so the work is extracted.** `pass1.py` is 658 lines against the 800 cap. Overlap retrieval and its diagnostic live in a new `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/overlap.py`; `_chunk_extra_context` gains only the call.\n\nAny ratcheted mechanism added carries a `# mechanism-ok:` marker naming this ticket at its definition site.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With `overlap=True`, reviewing a ticket whose plan restates an existing ticket's plan emits an advisory overlap finding naming that ticket. Checked by: a seeded-store test asserting the finding names that ticket id.\n- [ ] At most 5 candidates are injected into the Pass-1 extra context. Checked by: a test on a store seeded with over 5 matches asserting exactly 5 were injected.\n- [ ] With `overlap=True`, the number of LLM calls equals the number made by the same review with `overlap=False`. Checked by: a test comparing both call counts.\n- [ ] With `overlap=False`, no overlap finding is emitted. Checked by: a test asserting the finding set is empty.\n- [ ] With `overlap=False`, the run's checkpoint identity is byte-identical to the same review before this change. Checked by: a test comparing the computed identity against the unmodified path.\n- [ ] An overlap finding never changes a review's verdict from pass to block. Checked by: a test asserting a passing plan's verdict is unchanged with an overlap finding present.\n- [ ] `find_similar` called without `diagnostics` returns exactly what it returned before this change. Checked by: a test asserting the `recent_creates.py:196` call yields an unchanged result.\n- [ ] With no model provider configured, overlap retrieval still returns lexical-tier candidates. Checked by: a test with provider credentials cleared asserting a non-empty injected candidate set.\n- [ ] On each non-`ok` status (`index-absent`, `catch-up-failed`, `retrieval-error`) the verdict equals that of the same review with `overlap=False`. Checked by: one test per status comparing both verdicts.\n- [ ] `coverage[\"overlap\"][\"status\"]` records `index-absent` when the index is absent, `catch-up-failed` when catch-up raises, `retrieval-error` when retrieval raises. Checked by: one test per status asserting that value, with the overlap finding set empty.\n- [ ] Every module added or modified under `src/rebar/` is at most 800 lines. Checked by: the module-size gate.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0. Checked by: running it.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exits 0. Checked by: running it."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793692949960784001,"uuid":"832a1d10-a001-494c-a68c-dfde09196622"}